melody:
# Chorus (the original is in 2/4; written here with quarter-note beats)
Won't you come home, Bill Bai-ley, won't you come home?
D4 E4(2) G4 B4. A#4/ B4 D5 D4 E4(2) G4 B4(4)
She moans the whole day long;
D4 E4(2) G4 B4(2) D5(2) D5 ~F#4(3) ~F#4(2) r(2)
I'll do the cook-ing, dar-ling, I'll pay the rent;
D4 F#4(2) A4 C5 B4 C5 D5 D4 F#4(2) A4 C5(2) r(2)
I know I've done you wrong;
D4 F#4(2) A4 D5(2) E5(2) E5 ~B4(3) ~B4(2) r(2)
'Mem-ber that rain-y eve that I drove you out, with
D4 E4(2) G4 B4. A#4/ B4 D5 D4 E4(2) G4 B4(2) r D4
noth-ing but a fine tooth comb? I
D4 D4 G4 B4 D5(2) F5(2) E5(4) ~E5(2) r G4
know I'm to blame; well, ain't that a shame? Bill
G4 G4(2) G4 A4(2) G4(2) D5 D5(2) E5 B4(2) r B4
Bai-ley, won't you please come home?
B4 A4 G#4 A4 C5(2) B4(2) G4(4) ~G4(2) r(2)

